.TH S3M-CP 1 "" "s3m @VERSION@" "s3m Manual"
.SH NAME
s3m\-cp \- parallel copy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s3m\-cp
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fISOURCE\fR... \fIDEST\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copies objects and files in parallel.
Each SOURCE is an \fBs3://\fR URI (an exact key, or \fBPREFIX/\fR for its contents) or a local file or directory; DEST is an \fBs3://\fR URI or a local directory:
.TP
s3:// to s3://
server-side copy (no data through the client)
.TP
local to s3://
upload (multipart above 128 MiB)
.TP
s3:// to local directory
download (atomic temp file and rename)
.TP
local to local
refused; use p3m\-cp
.PP
By default this is a \fBdry run\fR listing what would be copied; add \fB\-\-apply\fR to copy.
.SS Destination rules
.IP \(bu 2
A prefix or directory SOURCE puts its contents under DEST.
.IP \(bu 2
An exact key or file with a DEST ending in \fB/\fR lands at DEST/\fIbasename\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
An exact key or file with any other DEST is copied to exactly that key or path (rename-style; single source only).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Actually copy.
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Replace existing destination objects or files.
Without it they are skipped and reported as \fBexists\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-move
Delete each source after its successful copy (batched DeleteObjects, or unlink for local files).
A failed copy never deletes its source.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " N"
Worker threads, 1\-256 (default 16).
.TP
.BI \-\-shard\-depth " N"
Prefix levels expanded for parallelism, 0\-9 (default 2).
.TP
.B \-\-rrdns
Resolve the endpoint hostname to every A/AAAA address and spread worker threads across them, moving a thread to the next address if its current one fails.
See
.BR s3m (7).
.TP
.B \-\-s3fs\-meta
On uploads, store each file's mode, mtime, uid and gid as the \fBx\-amz\-meta\-*\fR attributes s3fs reads, so the objects look native when the bucket is mounted with s3fs.
Without it s3fs falls back to default permissions and the upload time as mtime.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " FILE"
Write the CSV plan or report to FILE and show a live progress display.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the console listing; progress and the summary are still shown.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH NOTES
Objects over 5 GiB are copied server-side with multipart UploadPartCopy.
Copying a prefix into itself is refused.
Symbolic links in local sources are never followed.
.SH CONNECTION OPTIONS
The connection options \fB\-\-endpoint\fR, \fB\-\-region\fR, \fB\-\-profile\fR, \fB\-\-path\-style\fR, \fB\-\-no\-sign\fR, \fB\-\-insecure\fR and \fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fR are common to all s3m tools and are described in
.BR s3m (7).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 completed with errors; 2 usage, startup or safety-guard refusal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s3m (7)
.BR s3m\-sync (1),
.BR s3m\-rm (1)
